{{!
  Local override of the openapi-generator JavaSpring beanValidation template.

  Upstream emits @NotNull whenever the property is required, even when it is also
  nullable. For a required + nullable field (e.g. monthlyBudget, description) the
  generated getter ends up with @NotNull on a value the spec explicitly allows to
  be null ("Pass null to clear the budget."), so any null payload is rejected at
  the validation layer before reaching the controller.

  This override gates @NotNull behind ^isNullable so it is only emitted for
  required AND non-nullable properties. All other behavior (container @Valid and
  the beanValidationCore partial that emits @Min / @Size / @Pattern) is identical
  to upstream v7.22.0.

  Tracks upstream fix: https://github.com/OpenAPITools/openapi-generator/pull/14766
  Drop this override once that PR merges and the contracts repo bumps the
  generator version.
}}
